            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An implantable medical device comprising a backup system is provided. The backup system is adapted receive overriding control and/or power signals and wherein the signals indicate to the backup system to override a built-in control and/or powering system of the implantable medical device. The backup system, when being triggered, is arranged to override a built-in control and/or powering system of said implantable medical device, and the backup system is arranged to perform a predetermined emergency activity, the predetermined emergency activity being chosen from at least one of the following: running a motor, pumping using a pump, opening of an artificial restriction device on a bodily organ, releasing of a pharmaceutical drug in the mammal body, emptying a luminal organ in the mammal body, and emptying a urine bladder.</p>
            </abstract>
